<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bosnian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1992">1992</a>–<a href="/years/1995">1995</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bosnian War was fought from 1992 to 1995 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a> after its declaration of independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>, among Bosniak, Bosnian Serb and Bosnian Croat forces. It saw the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarajevo">Sarajevo</a>, ethnic cleansing and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srebrenica">Srebrenica</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> of 1995. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> air strikes and Croatian-Bosniak offensives led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dayton-agreement">Dayton Agreement</a> of December 1995, which ended the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bosnian-war.jpg" alt="Bosnian War" width="320" height="223" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Bushido at bs.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Krupa_nakon_rata.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
